{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f72f14de-dd23-43b7-b5fb-5288e67c9df9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bea96ff24bc48f1a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9010-ropnvl1h/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9010-E002.md","content":"# KServe inference audit event emission and at-least-once delivery\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers inference audit logging in the KServe serving stack:\nevery inference request processed through a KServe endpoint emits a\nstructured audit event conforming to the published common audit event\nschema, and events are delivered to the cluster audit sink (the standard\ncluster logging forwarder interface) with at-least-once semantics that\nsurvive component restarts. It also implements the serving-side honoring of\nthe per-project inference auditing enablement setting that the Dashboard\ncontrol writes.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Emit one audit event per inference request handled by a KServe endpoint,\n  capturing caller identity, model/version, timestamp, and response status,\n  and never capturing request or response payloads.\n- Emit events that conform to the published common inference audit event\n  schema.\n- Deliver events to the cluster audit sink via the standard cluster logging\n  forwarder interface with at-least-once semantics.\n- Ensure no audit events are lost when a serving component restarts\n  (durable buffering or an equivalent mechanism in the delivery path, sized\n  and bounded during implementation).\n- Honor a per-project inference auditing enablement setting: audit event\n  emission for a project's inference endpoints is gated by that project's\n  setting, so administrators can enable/disable auditing per project.\n- Cover all inference traffic through KServe endpoints in both deployment\n  modes supported by the serving stack (serverless and raw deployment).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- For a sample of inference requests through a KServe endpoint, each\n  request produces exactly one audit event containing caller identity,\n  model/version, timestamp, and response status, and containing no request\n  or response payload data.\n- Emitted events validate against the published common audit event schema.\n- With the cluster logging forwarder configured as audit sink, events\n  arrive at the sink at least once per emitted event.\n- Restarting the serving component during active inference traffic does not\n  result in loss of audit events for requests processed before the restart.\n- With per-project auditing disabled for a project, inference requests to\n  that project's endpoints produce no audit events; with it enabled, they\n  produce events per the criteria above.\n- The change is covered by the existing build pipeline for the serving\n  stack (pipeline green on the merged change).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): Every inference request through a KServe endpoint emits an\n  audit event capturing caller identity, model/version, timestamp, and\n  response status (not payloads).\n- HLR-2 (P0): Audit events are delivered to the cluster audit sink with\n  at-least-once semantics and are not lost on component restart.\n- HLR-3 (P1, serving-side scope only): the per-project enablement setting\n  honored here is the configuration surface that the Dashboard control\n  writes; the user-facing Dashboard surface is tracked separately.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":29635,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9237710a8f900247","agent_id":"a76fe8965019b7c94","session_id":"d259959c-9f88-4e8b-bf9c-c556eba940a6","uuid":"a2d0df33-1527-4441-93f8-9bc0ddf55847","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:44:41.941Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9010"}
