{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4cb314af06ef4be","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9010-E004\n3\ttitle: Document enabling inference auditing and interpreting audit events\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9010\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: RHOAI Documentation\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9010-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9010-E002\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9010-E003\n14\tai_signals:\n15\t  change_specificity: 1\n16\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n17\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n18\t  existing_foundation: 1\n19\t  open_questions: 1\n20\t  external_dependency: 1\n21\t  human_process_gates: 0\n22\t  repo_access: 1\n23\t  architecture_claims: 1\n24\tinvestigation_signals: null\n25\tai_implementability: High\n26\tai_implementability_score: 7\n27\tjira_key: null\n28\tbranch: null\n29\tgated_by: null\n30\tgate_failure_impact: null\n31\t---\n32\t# Document enabling inference auditing and interpreting audit events\n33\t\n34\t## Description\n35\t\n36\tThis epic delivers the end-user documentation for inference audit logging:\n37\thow administrators enable and disable inference auditing (including the\n38\tper-project Dashboard control), where audit events are delivered (the\n39\tcluster audit sink via the standard cluster logging forwarder), and how to\n40\tinterpret the fields of an audit event against the published common audit\n41\tevent schema.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- New documentation topic covering:\n46\t  - What inference auditing captures (caller identity, model/version,\n47\t    timestamp, response status) and what it deliberately does not capture\n48\t    (payloads).\n49\t  - How to enable and disable inference auditing per project from the\n50\t    Dashboard, including the administrator access required.\n51\t  - Where audit events are delivered (cluster audit sink / cluster logging\n52\t    forwarder) and any prerequisites on the customer side (long-term\n53\t    storage and retention are customer-provided and out of scope for the\n54\t    product, per the strategy).\n55\t  - How to interpret audit events: field-by-field reference against the\n56\t    published common audit event schema and its version.\n57\t  - At-least-once delivery semantics and what restart-survivability means\n58\t    for audit completeness, so auditors understand the guarantee.\n59\t- Follow the Red Hat docs content process and toolchain for authoring and\n60\t  publishing the topic.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- A published documentation topic exists covering enabling/disabling\n65\t  inference auditing per project and interpreting inference audit events.\n66\t- The topic's field reference matches the published common audit event\n67\t  schema (correct fields, correct payload-exclusion statement, correct\n68\t  schema version).\n69\t- The documented enable/disable procedure matches the actual Dashboard\n70\t  control and the serving-side behavior.\n71\t- The documentation has been technically reviewed against the implemented\n72\t  behavior by someone from the implementing teams before publication.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-5 (P2): Documentation covers enabling auditing and interpreting\n77\t  events.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9aeeb7f74a537613","agent_id":"a5a3439f5231012ad","session_id":"d259959c-9f88-4e8b-bf9c-c556eba940a6","uuid":"3619f2af-5074-40e7-8f26-802783a69cfb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:47:30.160Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4cb314af06ef4be","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9010 decomposition"}
