{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-beaf04fd9bd55383","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9010-E003\n3\ttitle: Dashboard per-project control for inference auditing\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9010\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9010-E002\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 8\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Dashboard per-project control for inference auditing\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic delivers the administrator-facing control in the RHOAI Dashboard\n35\tthat enables and disables inference auditing per data science project.\n36\tAdministrators use this control to turn audit event emission on or off for\n37\ta project's inference endpoints; the setting is the per-project inference\n38\tauditing configuration that the serving stack honors when emitting audit\n39\tevents.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Add a per-project inference auditing enable/disable control to the\n44\t  Dashboard, following the Dashboard's existing patterns for per-project\n45\t  and per-component settings (the Dashboard reads and writes Kubernetes\n46\t  CRs and owns no data plane).\n47\t- Write the per-project audit enablement configuration that the\n48\t  serving-side inference auditing implementation consumes, using the\n49\t  configuration surface defined by that implementation.\n50\t- Reflect the current effective state of the per-project auditing setting\n51\t  in the control (round-trip: change the setting, reload, state persists).\n52\t- Restrict the control to administrator-level access consistent with the\n53\t  Dashboard's existing project-scoped RBAC behavior.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- An administrator can enable and disable inference auditing for a project\n58\t  from the Dashboard, and the chosen state persists and is displayed\n59\t  correctly on reload.\n60\t- The control writes the per-project inference auditing configuration that\n61\t  the serving stack honors — toggling the control changes whether audit\n62\t  events are emitted for that project's inference endpoints.\n63\t- The control is visible and mutable only to users with the intended\n64\t  administrator-level access; non-administrator project users cannot change\n65\t  it.\n66\t- The change is covered by the existing Dashboard build pipeline (pipeline\n67\t  green on the merged change).\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-3 (P1): Administrators can enable/disable inference auditing per\n72\t  project from the Dashboard.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb49d0648fc7d8d0","agent_id":"a329e05d1a2384739","session_id":"d259959c-9f88-4e8b-bf9c-c556eba940a6","uuid":"1b04e4bd-354a-4aad-8522-27cb9d3bfc41","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:56:11.289Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-beaf04fd9bd55383","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9010 decomposition"}
